      "id": 1,
      "text": "Little Italy in San Diego began as a fishing village in the early 20th century, where Italian families worked in the tuna industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://sandiegopoi.com/little-italy/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The construction of Interstate 5 in the 1970s sliced through the heart of Little Italy, sparking a period of decline.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://sandiegopoi.com/little-italy/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Italian immigrants settled in the 1880s, many building San Diego’s railroads and working in stone quarries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.thelazyitalian.com/exploring-americas-little-italies/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Today, Mulberry Street remains the neighborhood’s core, lined with old‑world trattorias and pastry shops that echo its heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.thelazyitalian.com/exploring-americas-little-italies/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Little Italy blends historic charm with modern urban sophistication, offering a unique community feel that attracts locals and visitors alike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://sandiegopoi.com/little-italy/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The area’s historic buildings stand beside trendy cafés and boutique shops, creating a vibrant mix of old and new.",
